{"actor":"model","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-219661","model_call":14,"attempt":1,"model":"gpt-5.5","usage":{"input_tokens":7832,"output_tokens":317,"total_tokens":8149,"cached_tokens":6912,"reasoning_tokens":117},"output_characters":789,"decision":{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_39_866237787#0_1763779106","relevance":3,"reason":"The EPA page is dedicated to methyl bromide phaseout and directly states that methyl bromide is a fumigant used against agricultural pests including nematodes, depletes the ozone layer, and was phased out in the U.S. and other countries. This is direct evidence for loss of a major nematicide/fumigant due to environmental regulation.","learned":"Methyl bromide was lost/phased out because it depletes the ozone layer, with only critical-use and quarantine/preshipment exceptions."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1482","reason":"The methyl bromide query is producing authoritative direct evidence; continue to find more documents tying fumigant/nematicide loss to ozone-depletion phaseout."}}}
