{"actor":"model","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-219661","model_call":27,"attempt":1,"model":"gpt-5.5","usage":{"input_tokens":14142,"output_tokens":364,"total_tokens":14506,"cached_tokens":13056,"reasoning_tokens":146},"output_characters":912,"decision":{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_41_264265355#10_615472220","relevance":1,"reason":"The passage is related because it identifies Nemacur/fenamiphos as a formerly registered nematicide that was withdrawn from the market, but it does not explain the broader multi-decade loss of nematicides or give a clear regulatory/health/environmental cause; the only stated issue is declining efficacy before withdrawal.","learned":"Nemacur was once an important registered nematicide in California turf/golf contexts and was later withdrawn from the market, but the snippet does not state the regulatory reason."},"action":{"op":"document","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_41_264265355#10_615472220","reason":"The document may contain broader context on older nematicide withdrawals and the emergence of replacement products; inspect full text for direct causes such as regulatory, health, or environmental concerns."}}}
