{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-219661","model_call":60,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ \"plant nematodes\" \"plant-parasitic nematodes\" nematodes) (+ \"chemical nematicides\" nematicides) (+ toxic toxicity environmental health) (+ banned withdrawn restricted))"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ \"plant nematodes\" \"plant-parasitic nematodes\" nematodes) (+ \"chemical nematicides\" nematicides) (+ toxic toxicity environmental health) (+ banned withdrawn restricted))"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_51_1716969794#5_3210664013","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1519","rank":1,"snippet":"Vegetables (including Herbs) Plant Protection Products Occupational exposure to chemicals and reproductive health Male effects Aldicarb Uses Lawn and Turf 47.2.2.3 Nematodes and Nematicides Recommended publications \" , \"segment\": \"In different countries, different ranges of fumigants (e.g. methyl bromide and dichloropropene), precursors of fumigants (e.g. dazomet) and nonvolatile nematicides (in granular form such as aldicarb) are still authorized for use but the list is becoming more and more restricted because of the negative <cover>environmental impact of the chemicals. Methylbromide, for example, which has a remarkably wide-spectrum activity (including weeds, soil fungi, nematodes and insects), will be banned in all countries of the European Union in 2005. Nematicides </cover>protect young plantlets during the first stages of their development and allow their satisfactory installation and subsequent productivity. None the less, none of the nematicides can eradicate nematodes from the soil because individuals can usually survive in deeper levels where they can escape chemical diffusion; reinfestation of the plants will inevitably occur after a few months or years. It is absolutely necessary that preplanting chemical treatments, which act only against nematode stages surviving in the bare soil, are combined with the use of ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_51_1716969794#5_3210664013","rank":1,"relevance":3}]},"time":78},"model_calls":60,"document_judgments":31,"relevance_3":15,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
{"actor":"server","event":"request","topic_id":"2024-219661","model_call":60,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1519"},"model_calls":60,"document_judgments":31,"relevance_3":15,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-219661","model_call":60,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1519"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q1519"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_51_1716969794#4_3210661262","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1519","rank":2,"snippet":"Soil Nematicides Applying soil nematicides is justified when severe attacks are observed (high nematode densities in the previous crop) and in cases of replant sickness symptoms following repeated rose crops in the same field or greenhouse. In different countries, different ranges of fumigants (e.g. methyl bromide and dichloropropene), precursors of fumigants (e.g. dazomet) and nonvolatile nematicides (in granular form such as aldicarb) are still authorized for use but the list is becoming more and more restricted because of the negative <cover>environmental impact of the chemicals. Methylbromide, for example, which has a remarkably wide-spectrum activity (including weeds, soil fungi, nematodes and insects), will be banned in all countries of the European Union in 2005. Nematicides </cover>protect young plantlets during the first stages of their development and allow their satisfactory installation and subsequent productivity. None the less, none of the nematicides can eradicate nematodes from the soil because individuals can usually survive in deeper levels where they can escape chemical diffusion; reinfestation of the plants will inevitably occur after a few months or years.\" , \"start_char\": 3053.000000 , \"title\": \"Nematicide - an overview | ScienceDirect Topics\" , \"","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_51_1716969794#4_3210661262","rank":2,"relevance":3}]},"time":6},"model_calls":60,"document_judgments":31,"relevance_3":15,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
{"actor":"server","event":"request","topic_id":"2024-219661","model_call":60,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1519"},"model_calls":60,"document_judgments":31,"relevance_3":15,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-219661","model_call":60,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1519"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q1519"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_06_270229525#9_485579305","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1519","rank":3,"snippet":"important crops1 Side-effects Future developments References \" , \"segment\": \"Economic and <cover>environmental justification should be evaluated before use. The omission of compounds does not imply that they are not equally suitable for nematode control. 2 kg a.i./ha unless otherwise stated. Liquid fumigants EDB, metam-sodium and 1,3-D are applied to soil that has been prepared for planting. The soil surface is compacted with a roller after treatment which helps to seal the fumigant in the soil. Compounds releasing methyl isothiocyanate (dazomet, metam-sodium) work best in soils at >15°C. In cooler soils, the period between treatment and planting may have to be extended to allow sufficient time for the product to disperse. The liquid fumigant DBCP is the only volatile compound that can be applied to growing plants without causing phytotoxicity. However, its manufacture has now ceased for toxicological reasons and its use is banned in many countries. Non-volatile nematicides.\" , \"start_char\": 6627.000000 , \"title\": \"Chemical control of nematodes: </cover>efficiency and side-effects\" , \"url\": \"http://www.fao.org/3/v9978e/","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_06_270229525#9_485579305","rank":3,"relevance":3}]},"time":7},"model_calls":60,"document_judgments":31,"relevance_3":15,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
