{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-219661","model_call":73,"request":{"op":"document","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_15_1797328243#10_3591147408"},"record":{"query":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_15_1797328243#10_3591147408","op":"document"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_15_1797328243#10_3591147408","document":"ENY-012/NG005: Nematode Management in the Vegetable Garden ... Nematode Management in the Vegetable Garden 1 Nematode Management in the Vegetable Garden 1 What are nematodes? How do nematodes damage plants? Root-Knot Nematodes Ectoparasites Other Nematodes How do I know if nematodes are a problem? Handling Submitting a Sample What can I do about nematodes? Chemical Nematicides Bionematicides Resistance and Tolerance Soil Solarization Cover Crops Organic Amendments Planting Soil Tillage and Root Destruction Container Growing Summary Tables  ... Panel D, Theresa Friday UF/IFAS Extension How do nematodes damage plants? As plant-parasitic nematodes feed, they damage the root system and reduce the ability of a plant to obtain water and nutrients from the soil. When nematode numbers get high, and/or when environmental stresses occur, aboveground symptoms may become evident. Aboveground nematode symptoms often resemble nutrient deficiencies or drought stress. Symptoms include yellowing, wilting, and stunting (Figure 7, 8, 9). Figure 7. Nematode-damaged corn is stunted, yellow, and wilting. Damage occurs in patches. Credit: D. W. Dickson, UF/IFAS Figure 8.","ok":true,"op":"document"},"time":12},"model_calls":73,"document_judgments":34,"relevance_3":15,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
