{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-219661","model_call":78,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ nematicide nematicides) (+ \"environmental and health concerns\" \"health and environmental concerns\") (+ withdrawn banned deregistered restricted))"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ nematicide nematicides) (+ \"environmental and health concerns\" \"health and environmental concerns\") (+ withdrawn banned deregistered restricted))"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_00_1667865910#17_2916728807","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1534","rank":1,"snippet":"soil fumigants, while effective treatments for other plant-parasitic nematodes in Florida, often are not recommended for management of Nanidorus minor. Continuous cultivation of highly susceptible crops such as corn or sorghum can build up populations of P. minor to damaging numbers and may require the use of nematicides on subsequent crops. Summer legumes such as velvetbean or cowpea tend to keep populations of P. minor low and may reduce reliance on nematicides. In the past, organophosphate and carbamate nematicides such as aldicarb and fenamiphos were very effective for management of Nanidorus minor. However, these <cover>nematicides have been withdrawn due to environmental and health concerns. </cover>For current nematicide recommendations go to the UF EDIS webpage at https://edis.ifas.ufl.edu/. Selected References Christie JR, Perry VG. 1951. A root disease of plants caused by a nematode of the genus Trichodorus. Science 113:491-493. Decreamer W. 1991.\" , \"start_char\": 6918.000000 , \"title\": \"EENY339/IN616: Stubby-Root Nematode, Nanidorus minor (Colbran) Siddiqi (syn. Paratrichodorus minor, P. christiei, Trichodorus minor, T. christiei) (Nematoda: Adenophorea: Triplonchida: Diphtherophorina: Trichodoridea: Trichodoridae)\" , \"url\": \"http://edis.ifas.ufl.","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_00_1667865910#17_2916728807","rank