{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-219661","model_call":99,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ \"plant-parasitic nematodes\" \"plant parasitic nematodes\") (+ \"chemical control\" nematicides) (+ \"methyl bromide\" dbcp aldicarb) (+ banned withdrawn phaseout toxicity environmental))"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ \"plant-parasitic nematodes\" \"plant parasitic nematodes\") (+ \"chemical control\" nematicides) (+ \"methyl bromide\" dbcp aldicarb) (+ banned withdrawn phaseout toxicity environmental))"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_00_1667865910#16_2916726411","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1549","rank":1,"snippet":"8 to 16 inches deep, below the typical treatment zone of soil fumigants. This allows many Nanidorus minor to escape being killed by fumigant treatments. Population numbers of this nematode are known to rebound following soil fumigation to numbers higher than if no treatment were used. Therefore, soil fumigants, while effective treatments for other <cover>plant-parasitic nematodes in Florida, often are not recommended for management of Nanidorus minor. Continuous cultivation of highly susceptible crops such as corn or sorghum can build up populations of P. minor to damaging numbers and may require the use of nematicides on subsequent crops. Summer legumes such as velvetbean or cowpea tend to keep populations of P. minor low and may reduce reliance on nematicides. In the past, organophosphate and carbamate nematicides such as aldicarb and fenamiphos were very effective for management of Nanidorus minor. However, these nematicides have been withdrawn </cover>due to environmental and health concerns.\" , \"start_char\": 6216.000000 , \"title\": \"EENY339/IN616: Stubby-Root Nematode, Nanidorus minor (Colbran) Siddiqi (syn. Paratrichodorus minor, P. christiei, Trichodorus minor, T. christiei) (Nematoda: Adenophorea: Triplonchida: Diphtherophorina: Trichodoridea: Trichodoridae)\" , \"url\": \"","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_00_1667865910#16_2916726411","rank":1,"relevance":3}]},"time":77},"model_calls":99,"document_judgments":42,"relevance_3":18,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
